2026-10-12T19:39:19.4263610Z @@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
2026-10-12T19:39:19.4263811Z +# status Worker service
2026-10-12T19:39:19.4264018Z +
2026-10-12T19:39:19.4265214Z +Generated from the API template. The Worker owns `cloudflare.config.ts` and uses the shared contracts and observability packages. Storage: Volatile sample — resets when the Worker restarts. No resource provisioning runs during setup or build.
2026-10-12T19:39:19.4266310Z +
2026-10-12T19:39:19.4266511Z +From the workspace root:
2026-10-12T19:39:19.4266727Z +
2026-10-12T19:39:19.4266896Z +```console
2026-10-12T19:39:19.4267084Z +pnpm dev -- status
2026-10-12T19:39:19.4267337Z +pnpm --filter @independent-service/status test
2026-10-12T19:39:19.4268266Z +pnpm --filter @independent-service/status test:runtime
2026-10-12T19:39:19.4268857Z +pnpm --filter @independent-service/status build
2026-10-12T19:39:19.4269254Z +pnpm deploy:preflight -- --target status --environment local
2026-10-12T19:39:19.4269661Z +pnpm --filter @independent-service/status cf --help
2026-10-12T19:39:19.4269969Z +```
2026-10-12T19:39:19.4270138Z +
2026-10-12T19:39:19.4271470Z +`GET /status` reports `{ "ok": true, "service": "status" }` with `Cache-Control: no-store`; only that exact GET path is a status probe. `GET /health` reports readiness; the generated `/api/notes` sample validates input and creates, lists and deletes notes. Local writes are allowed. Remote artifacts deny unauthenticated writes; a service without D1 uses volatile memory and resets on restart.
2026-10-12T19:39:19.4272835Z +
2026-10-12T19:39:19.4274118Z +For approved dev delivery, configure an existing account/token and explicitly approved domain in the sole config, plus IDs for any selected resources. Run the dev preflight, then the workspace's checked `deploy` entry with its approved health URL. Local preflight/build do not establish remote deployment or connectivity. See [Cloudflare instructions](../../docs/cloudflare.md).
